@namespace AuthWithAdmin.Client.Components

@*
    MAdminBack — the Management area's one way back.

    WHAT THIS REPLACED, AND WHY
    ───────────────────────────
    This component started life as MAdminCrumbs, a breadcrumb trail, and
    went through two visual attempts before landing here:

      • a 12px muted "ניהול ‹" — legible as a label, invisible as an
        affordance;
      • a 14px link with a violet-tinted pill on hover — which read as a
        status chip parked above the title.

    The pattern that actually worked was already in the product: the form
    editor's circular back arrow. It is compact, obviously a control,
    visually separate from the title, and neutral. So the trail is gone and
    this is that arrow, standardized — ONE affordance across Management,
    not a breadcrumb and an arrow competing.

    HIERARCHY, NOT HISTORY
    ──────────────────────
    Href is always an explicit parent route. A top-level Management screen
    goes to /management; a detail screen goes to its own list
    (/management/cycles/{id} → /management/cycles). history.back() would
    send a user who arrived by link or bookmark somewhere unrelated, and
    would make the same arrow mean different things on the same screen.

    RTL AND THE ARROW'S DIRECTION
    ─────────────────────────────
    The glyph points RIGHT. In an RTL layout the direction a reader travels
    to get back to a parent is rightward, toward where the line began — the
    arrow names the destination's direction, so it points the way the click
    will take you.

    ACCESSIBLE NAME
    ───────────────
    The control is icon-only by design: the arrow beside the title is
    enough on screen, and a "חזרה לניהול" label beside every page title
    would be noise. So the name is carried by aria-label/title, composed
    from the destination — "חזרה לניהול", "חזרה לטפסים", "חזרה למחזורים
    אקדמיים" — which is also what a screen reader announces.
*@

<a class="@RootClass" href="@Href" title="@AccessibleName" aria-label="@AccessibleName">
    <svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
         stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M5 12h14" />
        <path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7" />
    </svg>
</a>

@code {
    /// <summary>The explicit parent route. Defaults to the Management hub,
    /// which is what every top-level Management screen wants.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string Href { get; set; } = "management";

    /// <summary>The destination's own name, used to build the accessible
    /// label. "ניהול" → "חזרה לניהול".</summary>
    [Parameter] public string Label { get; set; } = "ניהול";

    /// <summary>Overrides the composed label outright, for a destination
    /// whose name does not take a bare ל- prefix cleanly.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? AriaLabel { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public string? Class { get; set; }

    private string AccessibleName =>
        string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(AriaLabel) ? $"חזרה ל{Label}" : AriaLabel!;

    private string RootClass =>
        "m-admin-back" + (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Class) ? "" : $" {Class}");
}
